WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
- On this week to celebrate
our season three premier,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.340
we've been asking some L.A. celebrities

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.499
to share their L.A. Top Three.

00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:08.232
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:09.947
♪ L.A. Top Three ♪

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:12.738
(audience applauds)

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:13.860
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.850
- These are personalized
picks from our friends

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.280
who have lived here for years.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.280
Not your usual L.A. spots that you'll find

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.840
on an internet search.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.650
Today's Top Three comes from
one of the funniest guys ever,

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.740
let's head out to the field
where meteorologist...

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.710
I don't get to say that word a lot,

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.450
and I like the word meteorologist,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.283
I don't know why.
(audience laughs)

00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.610
Meteorologist. Melissa McGee from our...

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.350
Meteorologist Melissa McGee.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.930
Come on, all the M's.
(audience cheers)

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.983
From our partner station,
NBC for Los Angeles,

00:00:37.869 --> 00:00:38.819
she's standing by.

00:00:38.819 --> 00:00:41.720
What's up, Melissa?
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.250
- Hey, Kelly! It's so
nice to see you again!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.250
- It's nice to see you, too!

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.310
You were destined for it.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.950
Meteorologist Melissa
McGee, it was all destiny.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.450
- A lot of M's, yes.
- Yes.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.850
I like it, I like it.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.370
Will you introduce us to
the secret celebrity curator

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.850
of today's L.A. Top Three list?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.100
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.160
And you know, we're in
gorgeous, sunny Santa Monica

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.240
and I'm gonna reveal to you
where we are in just a moment,

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.790
but I do wanna tell you first,
that we've got a marine layer

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.130
that's starting to burn on off.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.950
That sun is coming out, people are happy,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.030
and the forecast calls
for a delicious lunch.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.497
And to tell you more about that,

00:01:16.497 --> 00:01:17.330
(Kelly yells)

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.199
I've got the one, the only,
here he is, the man himself,

00:01:20.199 --> 00:01:22.576
(audience cheers)
Arsenio Hall!

00:01:22.576 --> 00:01:23.597
- [Kelly] Let's go, Arsenio!

00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:25.186
- Let's get it. Elbows bump.
- Yes.

00:01:25.186 --> 00:01:26.458
- Thank you.
- I always do this.

00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:28.017
(Kelly cheers and laughs)

00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:30.847
- Our favorite meteorologist, Melissa.

00:01:30.847 --> 00:01:32.317
(audience cheers)
Yes.

00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.438
- [Melissa] Good to see you.

00:01:33.438 --> 00:01:34.620
- Good to see you.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.060
- My whole audience is doing it, man.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.100
You left an impact.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.542
- [Arsenio] Oh, that's so...
(Arsenio laughs)

00:01:40.542 --> 00:01:42.240
- Arsenio, I know how much you love L.A.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.030
So, how long have you lived here?

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.070
- I've been here too long!
You know how old I am!

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.498
I came here from Cleveland in 19...

00:01:48.498 --> 00:01:51.450
(Arsenio mumbles)
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.150
But I'm here now, and I got my
three secret places for you.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:55.983
- Okay,
(audience applauds)

00:01:55.983 --> 00:01:58.010
well, we're talking about best spots

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.430
for a leisurely lunch today,

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.610
so what are Arsenio Hall's

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.480
top three secret leisurely
lunches in Los Angeles?

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.480
Start with number three.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.780
- Okay, number three.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.780
I accidentally promised my girlfriend

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.418
that I wouldn't eat meat
until the pandemic was over.

00:02:11.418 --> 00:02:14.378
(Kelly laughs)
That was a mistake.

00:02:14.378 --> 00:02:18.300
A huge mistake, but it
lead me to great places.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.430
I found a wonderful vegan restaurant,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.840
my little hideout downtown,

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.330
and it's called Âu Lac, okay?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.883
And it's vegetarian,

00:02:28.775 --> 00:02:29.960
and I love the chef there.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.740
His name is Chef Ito.
- [Kelly] Ooh!

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.550
- Chef Ito made a vow to
silence many, many years ago,

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.900
and it he doesn't speak.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.640
So if you go there, he's not dissing you,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.370
he just doesn't speak.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.815
He can speak, but he doesn't.

00:02:42.815 --> 00:02:43.648
- What?

00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:44.880
- [Arsenio] He makes
incredible vegan stuff.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.870
Yeah, well, see. You and I love to talk,

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.520
and you'd love this chef,
because I talk to him,

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.904
and he don't say nothing back.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:52.737
- [Kelly] He'd listen.

00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:53.780
- And I dominate the conversation.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.180
(Kelly laughs and claps)
(audience applauds)

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.260
- That's my kind of date.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.010
All right, wait. What's number two?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.730
- Number two, sometimes
if you drive down PCH,

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.388
way, way, way, way down PCH,

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.020
(kelly giggles)

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.870
there's a place called Spruzzo.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.480
A wonderful Italian place.
They have great food,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.930
but I rarely get to the
food 'cause I like bread.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.660
They have the best bread, Kelly!

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.855
And I just eat bread for like
a hour and have cocktails.

00:03:22.855 --> 00:03:24.270
(audience applauds)
You can see the beach.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.180
It's an incredible place. Try Spruzzo's.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.730
- I want that pizza!

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:33.010
- And here we are at my number
one secret lunch location,

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.040
El Cholo, Clarkson!
(audience cheers)

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.450
Yeah, baby!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.960
It's near Wilshire at 11th,
but you have to enter on 11th

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.150
on the side.
- [Kelly] Mm.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.230
- [Arsenio] Kinda off the beaten path,

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.180
another one of my secret locations.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.780
This is my favorite dish.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.143
It's a crab meat enchilada.
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:52.267
(audience exclaims)
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.185
- [Arsenio] They also make
my favorite margarita.

00:03:55.185 --> 00:03:56.018
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:03:56.018 --> 00:03:58.420
- [Arsenio] And it's a
Cadillac Margarita with heat!

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.253
- [Kelly] Yes!
(audience applauds)

00:03:59.253 --> 00:04:01.023
- [Arsenio] So they put jalapeños in it.

00:04:01.023 --> 00:04:01.856
- Oh my God.

00:04:01.856 --> 00:04:02.689
- [Arsenio] And it gets you there, Kelly.

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:04.630
If you ever sit with writers
and wanna write jokes,

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.481
this is the fluid that
will make you funny.

00:04:07.481 --> 00:04:09.500
(Kelly laughs and claps)
(audience applauds)

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.600
- [Arsenio] Me and Owen
Smith, all the guys come here,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.480
and it's crazy. Anyway,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.011
Melissa, come on in.

00:04:15.011 --> 00:04:15.844
- Yes, I'm dying!

00:04:15.844 --> 00:04:16.990
- Our favorite meteorologist.
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.110
- She says there's a track of warm air

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.210
coming from the north, y'all.
(Melissa laughs)

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.960
So, get ready for it.
- Dying to try it.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.125
- [Kelly] I don't mind the gloomy.

00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:23.958
- [Arsenio] You gotta try it.

00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:24.791
- I don't mind the gloomy, it's good.

00:04:24.791 --> 00:04:26.030
That meal looks amazing

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.230
and I can't stand y'all right
now 'cause I'm not there.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.761
But it is always good to
see you Arsenio and Melissa.

00:04:30.761 --> 00:04:33.199
(audience cheers)
Thank you so much!

